Tetrapropyl Orthosilicate (TPS) is an organic silicon ester belonging to the orthosilicate family. Its molecular architecture features a silicon atom bonded to four propoxy groups, which confers strong hydrolysis and condensation activity. In sol‑gel chemistry TPS serves as a versatile silicon source for aerogels, inorganic coatings, silicone rubbers, optical components and electronic materials, enabling precise control over silica network formation.
