What is Tetrapropyl Orthosilicate?
Tetrapropyl Orthosilicate is a high‑purity organosilicate that is widely employed in sol‑gel processes to generate silica‑based networks. Its rapid and controllable hydrolysis makes it especially valuable for low‑dielectric‑constant (low‑k) materials used in modern semiconductor manufacturing, as well as for high‑performance protective coatings in aerospace, automotive and marine applications. The product is typically supplied in liquid form, with purity grades of 98 % and 99 % catering to different end‑use requirements.
